    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">KMg&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;30&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R080059 | R070367</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Chayesite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Chayesite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Velde D, Medenbach O, Wagner C, Schreyer W (1989) Chayesite, K(Mg,Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;[Si&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;30&lt;/sub&gt;]: A new rock-forming silicate mineral of the osumilite group from the Moon Canyon (Utah) lamproite, American Mineralogist 74, 1368-1373</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Milarite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.CM.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Cyclosilicate: [Si6O18]12- 6-membered double rings (sechser-Doppelringe)</gsmin:strunzlabel>
