  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mineral</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"A mineral is an element or chemical compound that is normally crystalline and that has been formed as a result of geological processes." Nickel, Ernest H. (1995), The definition of a mineral,  The Canadian Mineralogist. 33 (3): 689-90.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An amount of mineral: denotes a single mineral (a unit cell) or an aggregation of single minerals. All subtypes of Mineral currently denote an aggregation, e.g. Quartz denotes an aggregation of quartz unit cells.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n1fd689c41a864089b476a4d481ba57bdb195"/>
