    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Averievite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Averievite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Vergasova L P, Starova G L, Filatov S K, Anan'ev V V (1998) Averievite Cu&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(VO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·&lt;i&gt;n&lt;/i&gt;MX - a new mineral of volcanic exhalations, Doklady Akademii Nauk 359, 804-807 Chemical formula revised: Starova G L, Krivovichev S V, Fundamensky V S, Filatov S K (1997) The crystal structure of averievite, Cu&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(VO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·&lt;i&gt;n&lt;/i&gt;MX: comparison with related compounds, Mineralogical Magazine 61, 441-446</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.BB.85</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions, without H2O, With only medium-sized cations, (OH, etc.):RO4 about 1:1</gsmin:strunzlabel>
