    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;Sb&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;[Si&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;Be&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;AlFe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;36&lt;/sub&gt;]</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Welshite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Welshite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Moore P B (1978) Welshite, Ca_2_Mg_4_Fe^3+^Sb^5+^O_2_[Si_4_Be_2_O_18_], a new member of the aenigmatite group, Mineralogical Magazine 42, 129-132 Chemical formula redefined from Ca_2_Mg_4_Fe^3+^Sb^5+^O_2_[Si_4_Be_2_O_18_] to Ca_4_Mg_9_Sb_3_O_4_[Si_6_Be_3_AlFe_2_O_36_]: Grew E S, Barbier J, Britten J, Halenius U, Shearer C K (2007) The crystal chemistry of welshite, a non-centrosymmetric (P1) aenigmatite-sapphirine-surinamite group mineral, American Mineralogist 92, 80-90</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Sapphirine</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.DH.40</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
