    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Rusakovite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Ankinovich E A (1960) A new vanadium mineral, rusakovite, Zapiski Vsesoyuznogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchestva 89, issue 4, 440-447 Fleischer M (1960) New mineral names, American Mineralogist 45, 1313-1317</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.DF.15</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions and H2O, With only medium-sized cations, (OH,etc.):RO4 &gt; 3:1</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Rusakovite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1960</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/potassic-arfvedsonite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Potassic-arfvedsonite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>K | Na | Fe | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">amphibole-group 4 Na</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">KNa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;)Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2003-043</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">KNa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R050516</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Potassic-arfvedsonite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Potassic-arfvedsonite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Pekov I V, Chukanov N V, Lebedeva Y S, Pushcharovsky D Y, Ferraris G, Gula A, Zadov A E, Novakova A A, Petersen O V (2004) Potassicarfvedsonite, KNa_2_Fe^2+^_4_Fe^3+^Si_8_O_22_(OH)_2_, a K-dominant amphibole of the arfvedsonite series from agpaitic pegmatites - Mineral data, structure refinement and disorder in the A site, Neues Jahrbuch für Mineralogie, Monatshefte 2004, 555-574 Name changed from potassicarfvedsonite: Hawthorne F C, Oberti R, Harlow G E, Maresch W V, Martin R F, Schumacher J C, Welch M D (2012) Nomenclature of the amphibole supergroup. American Mineralogist 97, 2031-2048</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amphibole</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/hohmannite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hohmannite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Fe | O | S | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/hohmannite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·8H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Grandfathered|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1918</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1918:3"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1918.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O(S&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·8H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Hohmannite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Hohmannite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Frenzel A (1888) XVII. Mineralogisches. 10. Hohmannit. 11. Amarantit. 12. Vorkommnisse von Ehrenfriedersdorf, Mineralogische und Petrographische Mittheilungen 9, 397-400 Chemical formula modified from Fe^3+^_2_(SO_4_)_2_(OH)_2_·7H_2_O: Scordari F (1978) The crystal structure of hohmannite, Fe_2_(H_2_O)_4_[(SO_4_)_2_O]·4(H_2_O) and its relationship to amarantite, Fe_2_(H_2_O)_4_[(SO_4_)_2_O]·3(H_2_O). Mineralogical Magazine 42, 144-146</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amarantite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.DB.30</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sulfate, selenate, etc. with additional anions and H2O, With only medium-sized cations; insular octahedra and finite units</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Hohmannite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1888</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicsetting/Plate_Spreading_Center_Setting">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dct:source xml:lang="en">CGI Event Environment vocabulary</dct:source>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Tectonic setting where new oceanic crust is being or has been formed at a divergent plate boundary. Includes active and inactive spreading centers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">plate spreading center setting</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicsetting/Tectonic_Setting"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/arthurite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Arthurite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Cu | Fe | As | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">arthurite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/arthurite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CuFe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(AsO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1964-002</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-376</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:376:6"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-376.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cu&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(As&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R060235</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Arthurite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Arthurite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Davis R J, Hey M H (1964) Arthurite, a new copper-iron arsenate from Cornwall, Mineralogical Magazine 33, 937-941 Chemical formula revised: Davis R J, Hey M H (1969) The cell-contents of arthurite redetermined, Mineralogical Magazine 37, 520-521</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Arthurite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.DC.15</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions and H2O, With only medium-sized cations, (OH, etc.):RO4 = 1:1 and &lt; 2:1</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Arthurite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1964-002</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/clairite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Clairite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>N | H | Fe | S | O</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/clairite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(NH&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1982-093</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Diammonium triironIII tetrasulfate trihydroxyl trihydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1056</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1056:2"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1056.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(N&lt;sup&gt;3-&lt;/sup&gt;H&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(S&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Clairite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Clairite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Martini J E J (1983) Lonecreekite, sabieite and clairite, new secondary ammonium ferric-iron sulphates from Lone Creek Fall Cave, near Sabie, eastern Transvaal, Annals of the Geological Survey of South Africa 17, 29-34</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.DF.55</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sulfate, selenate, etc. with additional anions and H2O, With large and medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Clairite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1982-093</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/rockmaterial/Gabbroic_Rock">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dct:source xml:lang="en">LeMaitre et al. 2002</dct:source>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Gabbroid that has a plagioclase to total feldspar ratio greater than 0.9 in the QAPF fraction. Includes QAPF fields 10*, 10, and 10'. This category includes the various categories defined in LeMaitre et al. (2002) based on the mafic mineralogy, but apparently not subdivided based on the quartz/feldspathoid content.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gabbroic rock</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/rockmaterial/Basic_Igneous_Rock"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/rockmaterial/Gabbroid"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/malanite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Malanite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Cu | Ir | Pt | S</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">cubic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">linnaeite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/malanite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cu&lt;sup&gt;1+&lt;/sup&gt;(Ir&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;Pt&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;)S&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1995-003</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Copper diplatinum tetrasulfide</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2551</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2551:1"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2551.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cu&lt;sup&gt;1+&lt;/sup&gt;(Ir&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;Pt&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;)S&lt;sup&gt;2-&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R070051</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Malanite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Malanite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Zuxiang Y (1996) Malanite - a new cupric platinum (Pt^3+^) and iridium (Ir^3+^) sulfide, Acta Geologica Sinica 70, 309-314</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Spinel</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>02.DA.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Metal sulfide (M:S = 3:4)</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Malanite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1995-003</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/cattiite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cattiite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Mg | P | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Mg&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·22H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2000-032</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Trimagnesium diphosphate docosahydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-11456</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:11456:7"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-11456.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Mg&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·22H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cattiite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Cattiite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Britviv S N, Ferraris G, Ivaldi G, Bogdanova A N, Chukanov N V (2002) Cattiite, Mg&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·22H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O, a new mineral from Zhelezny mine (Kovdor Massif, Kola Peninsula, Russia), Neues Jahrbuch für Mineralogie, Monatshefte 2002, 160-168</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.CE.50</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. without additional anions, with H2O, With only medium-sized cations, RO4:H2O about 1:2.5</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Cattiite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>2000-032</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/fleischerite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fleischerite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Pb | Ge | S | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">hexagonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">fleischerite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/fleischerite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pb&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Ge(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Trilead germanium disulfate hexahydroxyl trihydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1556</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1556:7"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1556.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pb&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Ge&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;(S&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R120043</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Fleischerite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Fleischerite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Frondel C, Strunz H (1960) Fleischerit und itoit, zwei neue germanium-mineralien von Tsumeb, Neues Jahrbuch für Mineralogie, Monatshefte 1960, 132-142</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Fleischerite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.DF.25</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
