  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/gianellaite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Gianellaite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>N | Hg | S | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">cubic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/gianellaite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Hg&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;N)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)(H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O)&lt;sub&gt;x&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1972-020</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Tetramercury sulfate dinitride</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1688</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1688:5"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1688.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">[(N&lt;sup&gt;3-&lt;/sup&gt;Hg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;](S&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)(H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O)&lt;sub&gt;&lt;i&gt;x&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Gianellaite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Gianellaite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Tunell G, Fahey J J, Daugherty F W, Gibbs G V (1977) Gianellaite, a new mercury mineral, Neues Jahrbuch für Mineralogie, Monatshefte 1977, 119-131 Chemical formula revised from (Hg_2_N)_2_(SO_4_) to [(NHg_2_)_2_](SO_4_)(H_2_O)_&lt;i&gt;x&lt;/i&gt;_: Cooper M A, Abdu Y A, Hawthorne F C, Kampf A R (2016) The crystal structure of gianellaite, [(NHg_2_)_2_](SO_4)_(H_2_O)_&lt;i&gt;x&lt;/i&gt;_, a framework of (NHg_4_) tetrahedra with ordered (SO_4_) groups in the interstices. Mineralogical Magazine 80, 869-875</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>03.DD.30</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Double-, Oxy- or Hydroxy-  halide with Hg</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Gianellaite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1972-020</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
