  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/galkhaite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Galkhaite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Hg | Cu | Cs | As | S</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">cubic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/galkhaite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Hg&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Cu)CsAs&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;S&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1971-029</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1643</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1643:4"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1643.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Hg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Cu&lt;sup&gt;1+&lt;/sup&gt;)Cs&lt;sup&gt;1+&lt;/sup&gt;As&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;S&lt;sup&gt;2-&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R070394</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Galkhaite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Galkhaite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Grudzen V S, Stepanov V I, Shumkova N G, Chernitsova M M, Yudin R N, Bryzgalov I A (1972) Galkhaite, HgAsS_2_, a new mineral from arsenic-antimony-mercury deposits of the USSR, Doklady Akademii Nauk SSSR 205, 1194-1197 Chemical formula revised from HgAsS_2_: Chen T T, Szymanski J T (1981) The structure and chemistry of galkhaite, a mercury sulfosalt containing Cs and Tl, The Canadian Mineralogist 19, 571-581 Chemical formula revised from (Cs,Tl,[box])(Hg,Cu,Zn,Tl)_6_(As,Sb)_4_S_12_: Biagioni C, Bindi L, Zaccarini F (2014) Crystal chemistry of mercury sulfosalts – galkhaite, (Hg_5+x_Cu_1-x_)Cs_1-x_As_4_S_12_ (x˜0): crystal structure and revision of the chemical formula. The Canadian Mineralogist 52, 873-882</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Tennantite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>02.GB.20</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Neso-sulfarsenite with additional S</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Galkhaite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1971-029</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/cesarferreiraite">
