    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Clino-ferro-ferri-holmquistite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Li | Fe | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">amphibole-group 1 Mg-Fe-Mn-Li</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;Li&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2001-066</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;Li&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Clino-ferro-ferri-holmquistite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Clino-ferro-ferri-holmquistite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Name defined by IMA nomenclature commission for the hypothetical mineral: Leake B E, Woolley A R, Arps C E S, Birch W D, Gilbert M C, Grice J D, Hawthorne F C, Kato A, Kisch H J, Krivovichev V G, Linthout K, Laird J, Mandarino J A, Maresch W V, Nickel E H, Rock N M S, Schumacher J C, Smith D C, Stephenson N C N, Ungaretti L, Whittaker E J W, Youzhi G (1997) Nomenclature of amphiboles: Report of the subcommittee on amphiboles of the International Mineralogical Association, commission on new minerals and mineral names, The Canadian Mineralogist 35, 219-246 Mineral discovered in nature: Oberti R, Cámara F, Caballero J M, Ottolini L (2003) Sodic-ferri-ferropedrizite and ferri-clinoferroholmquistite: mineral data and degree of order of the ?-site cations in Li-rich amphiboles, The Canadian Mineralogist 41, 1345-1354 Name changed from Ferri-clinoferroholmquistite: Hawthorne F C, Oberti R, Harlow G E, Maresch W V, Martin R F, Schumacher J C, Welch M D (2012) Nomenclature of the amphibole supergroup. American Mineralogist 97, 2031-2048</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amphibole</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/parwanite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Parwanite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Mg | Al | P | O | C | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaMg&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)(OH)&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;·30H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1986-036a</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-31409</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:31409:7"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-31409.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaMg&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)(OH)&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;·30H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Parwanite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Parwanite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Birch W D, Mills S J, Schwendtner K, Pring A, Webb J A, Segnit E R, Watts J A (2007) Parwanite: a new hydrated Na—Mg—Al-phosphate from a lava cave at Parwan, Victoria, Australia, Australian Journal of Mineralogy 13, 23-30</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.DO.40</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions and H2O, With CO3, SO4, SiO4</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Parwanite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1986-036a</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/clinohumite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Clinohumite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Mg | Si | O | F</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">humite-humite subgroup</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/clinohumite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Mg&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;(SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Grandfathered|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Nonamagnesium tetranesosilicate difluoride</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1077</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1077:7"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1077.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Mg&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;(SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R040122 | R050183 | R060559 | R070561</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Clinohumite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Clinohumite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Des Cloizeaux A L O L (1876) Über den humit; nur der I. Typus ist rhombisch, die beiden andern sind monoklin, doch mit verschiedenen grundformen, Neues Jahrbuch für Mineralogie, Geologie und Palaontologie 1876, 640-645</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Humite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.AF.55</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Nesosilicate with additional anions; cations in [4], [5] and/or only [6] coordination</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Clinohumite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1876</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/calcite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Calcite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | C | O</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">hexagonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">calcite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/calcite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Grandfathered|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Calcium carbonate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-859</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:859:4"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-859.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CaCO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R040070 | R040170 | R050048 | R050009 | R050127 | R050128 | R050130 | R050307 | R150020 | R150075</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Calcite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Calcite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Mineral known since antiquity under a number of names, but it appears to have first been called calcite in this publication: Freiesleben J C (1836) Calcit, Magazin für die Oryktographie von Sachsen 7, 118-121</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Calcite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>05.AB.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Carbonate without additional anions, without H2O, Alkali-earth (and other M2+) carbonates</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Calcite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>old</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/marthozite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Marthozite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Cu | U | O | Se | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">orthorhombic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/marthozite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cu&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;(UO&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Se&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·8H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1968-016</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: CopperII triuranyl diselenite dioxy octahydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2582</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2582:5"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2582.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cu&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;(UO&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Se&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·8H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R090052</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Marthozite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Marthozite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Cesbron F, Oosterbosch R, Pierrot R (1969) Une nouvelle espèce minérale: la marthozite. Uranyl-sélénite de cuivre hydraté, Bulletin de la Société Française de Minéralogie et de Cristallographie 92, 278-283 Fleischer M (1970) New mineral names, American Mineralogist 55, 533-535</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.JJ.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Selenite with additional anions and H2O</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Marthozite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1968-016</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
