    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">amphibole-group 2 Ca</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CaCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Al)(Si&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1993-033</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CaCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Al)(Si&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Fluoro-cannilloite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Fluoro-cannilloite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Hawthorne F C, Oberti R, Ungaretti L, Grice J D (1996) A new hyper-calcic amphibole with Ca at the A site: Fluor-cannilloite from Pargas, Finland, American Mineralogist 81, 995-1002 Name changed from fluor-cannilloite: Burke E A J, Leake B E (2005) “Named amphiboles”: a new category of amphiboles recognized by the International Mineralogical Association (IMA) and a defined sequence order for the use of prefixes in amphibole names, American Mineralogist 90, 516-517 Name changed back to fluor-cannilloite: Hawthorne F C, Oberti R, Harlow G E, Maresch W V, Martin R F, Schumacher J C, Welch M D (2012) Nomenclature of the amphibole supergroup. American Mineralogist 97, 2031-2048</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amphibole</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/nefedovite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nefedovite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Ca | P | O | F</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">tetragonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/nefedovite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Ca&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;F</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1982-048</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Pentasodium tetracalcium tetraphosphate tetrafluoride</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2870</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2870:3"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2870.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Ca&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;F</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Nefedovite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Nefedovite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Khomyakov A P, Nechelyustov G N, Dorokhova G I (1983) Nefedovite, Na5Ca4(PO4)4F, a new mineral, Zapiski Vsesoyuznogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchestva 112, issue 4, 479-483 Dunn P J, Fleischer M, Francis C A, Langley R H, Kissin S A, Shigley J E, Vanko D A, Zilczer J A (1984) New mineral names, American Mineralogist 69, 810-815</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.BO.30</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions, without H2O, With only large cations, (OH, etc.):RO4 about 1:1</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Nefedovite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1982-048</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/hundholmenite-y">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
