    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pseudorutile</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Pseudorutile</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Teufer G, Temple A K (1966) Pseudorutile - a new mineral intermediate between ilmenite and rutile in the natural alteration of ilmenite, Nature 211, 179-181 Discredited because of inadequate description: International Mineralogical Association (1968) International Mineralogical Association: Commission on new minerals and mineral names, Mineralogical Magazine 36, 1143-1145 Redefined: Grey I E, Watts J A, Bayliss P (1994) Mineralogical nomenclature: pseudorutile revalidated and neotype given, Mineralogical Magazine 58, 597-600</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Tivanite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.CB.25</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
