    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Trabzonite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Trabzonite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Sarp H, Burri G (1987) Yeni bir mineral, trabzonit, Ca&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; Si&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; O&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt; 2H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O, Bulletin of the Geological Society of Turkey 30, 57-60 Chemical formula revised: Armbruster T, Lazic B, Galuskina I O, Galuskin E V, Gnos E, Marzec K M, Gazeev V M (2012) Trabzonite, Ca&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;[Si&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)]OH: crystal structure, revised formula, new occurrence and relation to killalaite, Mineralogical Magazine 76, 455-472</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.BJ.15</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sorosilicate with Si3O10, Si4O11, etc. anions; cations in octahedral [6] and greater coordination</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Trabzonite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1983-071a</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/cardite">
