    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Senarmontite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Mineral described but not named: de Senarmont H H (1851) Note sur l´antimoine oxydé naturel de forme octaédrique, Annales de Chimie et de Physique 31, 504-507 Mineral named: Dana J D (1851) Mineralogical Notices. No. III. 1. New species. Octahedral oxyd of antimony, American Journal of Science and Arts 12, 205-222 Spelling of name changed from sénarmontite to senarmontite: Hålenius U, Hatert F, Pasero M, Mills S J (2015) IMA Commission on New Minerals, Nomenclature and Classification (CNMNC) Newsletter 28. New minerals and nomenclature modifications approved in 2015. Mineralogical Magazine 79, 1859-1864</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Arsenolite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.CB.50</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Oxide, Metal: Oxygen = 2: 3,3: 5, and similar, With medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Senarmontite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1851</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
