  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicsetting/Rocky_Coast_Setting">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dct:source xml:lang="en">North American Geologic-map Data Model Science Language Technical Team, 2004, Sedimentary materials:science language for their classification, description, and interpretation in digital geologic-map databases, Version 1.0 (12/18/2004): U.S. Geological Survey Open-File Report 2004-1451 appendix C, 595 p., accessed at http://pubs.usgs.gov/of/2004/1451/sltt/appendixC/</dct:source>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Shoreline with significant relief and abundant rock outcrop.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">rocky coast setting</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicsetting/Shoreline_Setting"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/shungite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Shungite is elementary noncrystalline carbon with a metastable structure incapable of graphitization.  Trace amounts of fullerenes (0.0001 &lt; 0.001%) have been reported from such rock (Mosin &amp; Ignatov, 2013). Shungite has a biogenic origin. (https://www.mindat.org/min-11040.html)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">shungite </rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineraloid_Material"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">shungite </skos:prefLabel>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>https://www.mindat.org/min-11040.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/phillipsite-na">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phillipsite-Na</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Si | Al | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">orthorhombic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">zeolite-phillipsite series</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;32&lt;/sub&gt;·12H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-7229</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:7229:4"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-7229.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;32&lt;/sub&gt;·12H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R061094 | R070271</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Phillipsite-Na</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Phillipsite-Na</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Levy A (1825) Descriptions of two new minerals, The Annals of Philosophy 10, 361-363 Name changed from phillipsite to the Na-dominant species originally found at Aci Castello, Sicily, Italy: Coombs D S, Alberti A, Armbruster T, Artioli G, Colella C, Galli E, Grice J D, Liebau F, Mandarino J A, Minato H, Nickel E H, Passaglia E, Peacor D R, Quartieri S, Rinaldi R, Ross M, Sheppard R A, Tillmanns E, Vezzalini G, (1997) Recommended nomenclature for zeolite minerals: report of the Subcommittee on Zeolites of the International Mineralogical Association, Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names, The Canadian Mineralogist 35, 1571-1606</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.GC.10</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Zeolite family: Chains of doubly-connected 4-membered rings</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Phillipsite-Na.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1825</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/atokite">
