    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Florencite-(La)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Mineral reported as a La-rich florencite, but not named: Lefebvre J J, Gasparrini C (1980) Florencite, an occurrence in the Zairian copperbelt, The Canadian Mineralogist 18, 301-311 Mineral named by IMA nomenclature commission: Nickel E H, Mandarino J A (1987) Procedures involving the IMA Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names and guidelines on mineral nomenclature, American Mineralogist 72, 1031-1042</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Alunite-crandallite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.BL.13</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions, without H2O, With medium-sized and large cations, (OH, etc.):RO4 = 3:1</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Florencite-%28La%29.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1980</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/pakhomovskyite">
