  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/charoite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Charoite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>K | Sr | Ba | Mn | Ca | Na | Si | O | H | F</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic, orthorhombic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/charoite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(K,Sr,Ba,Mn)&lt;sub&gt;15-16&lt;/sub&gt;(Ca,Na)&lt;sub&gt;32&lt;/sub&gt;[Si&lt;sub&gt;70&lt;/sub&gt;(O,OH)&lt;sub&gt;180&lt;/sub&gt;](OH,F)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;·nH&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1977-019</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-972</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:972:4"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-972.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(K,Sr,Ba,Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;15-16&lt;/sub&gt;(Ca,Na)&lt;sub&gt;32&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;70&lt;/sub&gt;(O,OH)&lt;sub&gt;180&lt;/sub&gt;(OH,F)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;·nH&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R060376 | R060557</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Charoite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Charoite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Rogova V P, Rogov Y G, Drits V A, Kuznetsova N N (1978) Charoite, a new mineral, and a new jewelry stone, Zapiski Vsesoyuznogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchestva 107(1), 94-100 Chemical formula revised: Nikishova L V, Lazebnik K A, Lazebnik Y D (1985) About the crystallochemical formula of charoite, in Crystal Chemistry and Structure of Minerals, Nauka (Leningrad, Russia) 100-105 Chemical formula revised again: Rozhdestvenskaya I, Mugnaioli E, Czank M, Depmeier W, Kolb U, Reinholdt A, Weirich T (2010) The structure of charoite, (K,Sr,Ba,Mn)&lt;sub&gt;15-16&lt;/sub&gt;(Ca,Na)&lt;sub&gt;32&lt;/sub&gt;[(Si&lt;sub&gt;70&lt;/sub&gt;(O,OH)&lt;sub&gt;180&lt;/sub&gt;)](OH,F)&lt;sub&gt;4.0&lt;/sub&gt;·nH&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O, solved by conventional and automated electron diffraction, Mineralogical Magazine 74, 159-177</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.DG.92</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Inosilicate with 3-periodic single and multiple chains</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Charoite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1977-019</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/ammoniovoltaite">
