    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Britvinite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Chukanov N V, Yakubovich O V, Pekov I V, Belakovsky D I, Massa A (2007) Britvinite, Pb&lt;sub&gt;15&lt;/sub&gt;Mg&lt;sub&gt;9&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;28&lt;/sub&gt;)(BO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; - a new mineral from Långban, Sweden, Zapiski Rossiiskogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchetstva 136(6), 18-25 Chemical formula revised: Yakubovich O V, Massa W, Chukanov N V (2008) Crystal structure of britvinite [Pb&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;F(BO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)][Mg&lt;sub&gt;4.5&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;14&lt;/sub&gt;)]: A new layered silicate with an original type of silicon-oxygen networks, Crystallography Reports 53, 206-215</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Molybdophyllite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.EG.70</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
