    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2097:4"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2097.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">BaNaFe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;F</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R060580 | R061018</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Jinshajiangite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Jinshajiangite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Hong W, Fu P (1982) Jinshajiangite, a new Ba-Mn-Fe-Ti-bearing silicate mineral, Geochemistry 1, 458-464 Chemical formula changed from (Na,K)_5_(Ba,Ca)_4_(Fe^2+^,Mn)_15_(Ti,Fe^3+^,Nb)_8_(SiO_4_)_15_(F,O,OH)_10_: Rastsvetaeva R K, Chukanov N V, Rozenberg K A (2008) Crystal structure of jinshajiangite from the Norra Kärr Complex (Sweden), Crystallography Reports 53, 553-556 Chemical formula changed from Na_2_KCaBa(Fe^2+^,Mn)_8_Ti_4_Si_8_O_32_(O,F)_6_: Sokolova E, Camara F, Hawthorne F C, Abdu Y (2009) From structure topology to chemical composition. VII. Titanium silicates: the crystal structure and crystal chemistry of jinshajiangite, European Journal of Mineralogy 21, 871-883</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Seidozerite-Bafertisite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.BE.67</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sorosilicate: Si2O7 groups, with additional anions; cations in octahedral [6] and greater coordination</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Jinshajiangite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1981-061</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
