  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicunit/Allostratigraphic_Unit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">allostratigraphic unit</rdfs:label>
    <dct:source xml:lang="en">This vocabulary, Salvador, 1994, Donovon 2004 IUGS abstract.</dct:source>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Geologic unit defined by bounding surfaces. Not necessarily stratified. Donovon (2004, IUGS abstract Florence) makes good case for use of a noncommittal term for the bounding surface. While there may be no agreement that a given stratal boundary is a discontinuity, there is consensus that all the identified boundaries are stratal surfaces. Includes: 1. Unconformity bounded units (Salvador 1994), defined by bounding stratigraphic discontinuities ('significant unconformities', unconformity is defined as surface of erosion in Salvador 1994). 2. Sequence stratigraphic unit, an allostratigraphic unit that is used to interpret the depositional origin of sedimentary strata and assumes, though this is not always stated, an implicit connection to base level change. It does this by establishing how the sequence of strata accumulated in order in the sedimentary section over a subdividing framework of surfaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicunit/Stratigraphic_Unit"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/hellandite-y">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hellandite-(Y)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | REE | Y | Al | B | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">hellandite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/hellanditey.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca,REE)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Y&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(B&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;)(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2000-F</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1852</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1852:0"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1852.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca,REE)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Y&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(B&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;)(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Hellandite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Hellandite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Brøgger W C (1903) Über den hellandit, ein neues mineral, Nyt Magazin for Naturvidenskabena 41, 213-221 Name changed from hellandite: Nickel E H, Mandarino J A (1987) Procedures involving the IMA Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names and guidelines on mineral nomenclature, American Mineralogist 72, 1031-1042 Chemical formula redefined: Oberti R, Ventura G D, Ottolini L, Hawthorne F C, Bonazzi P (2002) Re-definition, nomenclature, and crystal-chemistry of the hellandite group, American Mineralogist 87, 745-752</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Hellandite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.DK.20</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Inosilicate with 5-periodic single chains</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Hellandite-%28Y%29.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1903</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
