    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Bredigite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Bredigite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Tilley C E, Vincent H C G (1948) The occurrence of an orthorhombic high-temperature form of Ca&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; (bredigite) in the Scawt Hill contact-zone and as a constituent of slags, Mineralogical Magazine 28, 255-271 Chemical formula revised: Moore P B, Araki T (1976) The crystal structure of bredigite and the genealogy of some alkaline earth orthosilicates, American Mineralogist 61, 74-87</gsmin:statusnotes>
