    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Berthier P (1819) Analyse de deux minéraux zincifères des États-Unis d´Amérique, Annales des Mines 4, 483-494</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Spinel</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.BB.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Oxide, Metal: Oxygen = 3:4 and similar, With only medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Franklinite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1819</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/kieserite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kieserite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Mg | S | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">kieserite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/kieserite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Mg(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)·H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Magnesium sulfate monohydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2204</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2204:6"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2204.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">MgS&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;·H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Kieserite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Kieserite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Reichardt E (1860) Das Steinsalzbergwerk Stassfurth Bei Magdeburg. Novorum Actorum Academiae Caesareae Leopoldino-Carolinae Germanicae Naturae Curiosorum 27, 609-659</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Kieserite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.CB.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sulfate, selenate, etc. without additional anions, with H2O, With only medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Kieserite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1861</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/wiklundite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Wiklundite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Pb | Mn | Zn | Fe | Mg | As | O | Si | H | Cl</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">hexagonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pb&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;,Zn)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;,Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;,Mg)&lt;sub&gt;19&lt;/sub&gt;(As&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;[(Si,As&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;18&lt;/sub&gt;Cl&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2015-057</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pb&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;,Zn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;,Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;,Mg)&lt;sub&gt;19&lt;/sub&gt;(As&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Si,As&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;18&lt;/sub&gt;Cl&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Wiklundite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Wiklundite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Cooper M A, Hawthorne F C, Langhof J, Hålenius U, Holtstam D (2017) Wiklundite, ideally Pb_2_^[4]^(Mn^2+^,Zn)_3_(Fe^3+^,Mn^2+^)_2_(Mn^2+^,Mg)_19_(As^3+^O_3_)_2_[Si,As^5+^)O_4_]_6_(OH)_18_Cl_6_, a new mineral from Långban, Filipstad, Värmland, Sweden: Description and crystal structure. Mineralogical Magazine 81, 841-855</gsmin:statusnotes>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/ganophyllite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ganophyllite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>K | Na | Mn | Si | Al | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">ganophyllite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/ganophyllite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(K,Na)&lt;sub&gt;x&lt;/sub&gt;Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(Si,Al)&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;24&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;·nH&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O (x = 1-2; n = 7-11)</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Grandfathered|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1649</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1649:6"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1649.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(K,Na)&lt;sub&gt;1-2&lt;/sub&gt;Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(Si,Al)&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;24&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;·7-11H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ganophyllite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Ganophyllite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Hamberg A (1890) Ueber Ganophyllit, ein Manganzeolith, von Harstigen. Geologiska Föreningens i Stockholm Förhandlingar 12, 586-598. Chemical formula revised, based on its isomorphism with tamaite: Hughes J M, Rakovan J, Bracco R, Gunter M E (2003) The atomic arrangement of the ganophyllite-group modulated layer silicates as determined from the orthorhombic dimorph of tamaite, with the elusive 16.8 Å ganophyllite-group superstructure revealed, American Mineralogist 88, 1324-1330</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Clay</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.EG.30</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phyllosilicate: Double nets with 6-membered and larger rings</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Ganophyllite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1890</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Geologic_Time_Feature">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Any geological temporal feature, including a geologic date, time interval, or time boundary. All geologic time features are dependent one some rock body, strongly or weakly.</rdfs:comment>
