    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Kimuraite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Nagashima K, Miyawaki R, Takase J, Nakai I, Sakurai K, Matsubara S, Kato A, Iwano S (1986) Kimuraite, CaY_2_(CO_3_)_4_·6H_2_O, a new mineral from fissures in an alkali olivine basalt from Saga Prefecture, Japan, and new data on lokkaite, American Mineralogist 71, 1028-1033 Name changed from kimuraite to kimuraite-(Y): Nickel E H, Mandarino J A (1987) Procedures involving the IMA Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names and guidelines on mineral nomenclature, American Mineralogist 72, 1031-1042</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Tengerite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>05.CC.15</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Carbonate without additional anions, with H2O, With rare earth elements (REE)</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Kimuraite-%28Y%29.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1984-073</gsmin:wikipediadate>
