    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Deliensite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Deliensite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Vochten R, Blaton N, Peeters O (1997) Deliensite, Fe(UO&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O, a new ferrous uranyl sulfate hydroxyl hydrate from Mas D'Alary, Lodève, Hérault, France, The Canadian Mineralogist 35, 1021-1025 Chemical formula revised: Plášil J, Hauser J, Petrícek V, Meisser N, Mills S J, Škoda R, Fejfarová K, Cejka J, Sejkora J, Hloušek J, Johannet J-M, Machovic V, Lapcák L (2012) Crystal structure and formula revision of deliensite, Fe[(UO_2_)_2_(SO_4_)_2_(OH)_2_](H_2_O)_7_, Mineralogical Magazine 76, 2837-2860</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.EB.10</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Uranyl sulfate, With medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
