  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/tinzenite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tinzenite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Mn | Al | B | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">axinite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/tinzenite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;[B&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;30&lt;/sub&gt;](OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-3972</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:3972:3"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-3972.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;[B&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;30&lt;/sub&gt;](OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R050251 | R110064</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Tinzenite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Tinzenite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Jakob J (1923) Vier Mangansilikate aus dem Val d'Err (Kt. Graubünden). Schweizerische Mineralogische und Petrographische Mitteilungen 3, 227-237 Tinzenite is identified as Ca-poor axinite and its chemical formula revised from H_2_Ca_3_Al_4_Mn^3+^_4_Si_8_O_32_ to H(Ca,Mn,Fe,Mg)_3_Al_2_BSi_4_O_16_: Milton C A, Hildebrand F A, Sherwood A M (1953) The identity of tinzenite with manganoan axinite. American Mineralogist 38, 1148-1158 Redefined: Sanero E, Gottardi G (1968) Nomenclature and crystal-chemistry of axinites, American Mineralogist 53, 1407-1411 Chemical formula revised from Ca_6_Al_4_[B_2_Si_8_O_30_](OH)_2_ to Ca_2_Mn^2+^_4_Al_4_[B_2_Si_8_O_30_](OH)_2_: Hålenius U, Hatert F, Pasero M, Mills S J (2016) IMA Commission on New Minerals, Nomenclature and Classification (CNMNC) Newsletter 32. New minerals and nomenclature modifications approved in 2016. Mineralogical Magazine 80, 915-922</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Axinite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.BD.20</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sorosilicate: Si2O7 groups, with additional anions; cations in tetrahedral [4] and greater coordination</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Tinzenite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1968</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/utahite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Utahite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Cu | Zn | Te | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/utahite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cu&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Zn&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Te&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;·7H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1995-039</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-7348</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:7348:2"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-7348.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cu&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Zn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Te&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;·7H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Utahite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Utahite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Roberts A C, Stirling J A R, Criddle A J, Jensen M C, Moffatt E A, Wilson W E (1997) Utahite, a new mineral and associated copper tellurates from the Centennial Eureka mine, Tintic District, Juab County, Utah, The Mineralogical Record 28, 175-179</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.DE.25</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sulfate, selenate, etc. with additional anions and H2O, With only medium-sized cations; unclassified</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Utahite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1995-039</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/almarudite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Almarudite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>K | Na | Mn | Fe | Mg | Be | Al | Si | O</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">hexagonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">milarite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">K(&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;,Na)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mn,Fe,Mg)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;[(Be,Al)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;]O&lt;sub&gt;30&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2002-048</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-25681</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:25681:8"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-25681.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">K(&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;,Na)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Be&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;30&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Almarudite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Almarudite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Mihajlovic T, Lengauer C L, Ntaflos T, Lolitsch U, Tillmanns E (2004) Two new minerals, rondorfite, Ca&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;Mg[SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Cl&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;, and almarudite, K([box],Na)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mn,Fe,Mg)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Be,Al)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;[Si&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;30&lt;/sub&gt;], and a study of iron-rich wadalite, Ca&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;[(Al&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;32&lt;/sub&gt;]C&lt;sub&gt;16&lt;/sub&gt;, from the Bellerberg (Bellberg) volcano, Eifel, Germany, Neues Jahrbuch für Mineralogie, Abhandlungen 179, 265-294</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Milarite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.CM.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Cyclosilicate: [Si6O18]12- 6-membered double rings (sechser-Doppelringe)</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Almarudite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>2002-048</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
