  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/zincohogbomite-2n6s">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Zincohögbomite-2&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;6&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Zn | Al | Fe | Ti | Mg | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">hexagonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">hogbomite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Zn,Al)&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;(Al,Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;,Ti,Mg)&lt;sub&gt;16&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;31&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Renamed|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-11444</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:11444:2"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-11444.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Zn&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;,Al)&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;(Al,Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;,Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;,Mg)&lt;sub&gt;16&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;31&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Zincohögbomite-2&amp;lt;i&amp;gt;N&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;6&amp;lt;i&amp;gt;S&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Zincohogbomite-2N6S</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Designated as zinc hoegbomite: Moleva V A, Miasnikov V S (1952) Hoegbomite and its variety - zinc hoegbomite, Doklady Akademii Nauk SSSR 83, 733-736 Designated as zincohögbomite-16H: Armbruster T, Bermanec V, Zebec V, Oberhänsli R (1998) Titanium and iron poor zincohögbomite-16H, Zn_14_(Al,Fe^3+^,Ti,Mg)_8_Al_24_O_62_(OH)_2_, from Nezilovo, Macedonia: occurrence and crystal structure of a new polysome, Schweizerische Mineralogische und Petrographische Mitteilungen 78, 469-477 Name and chemical formula revised: Armbruster T (2002) Revised nomenclature of högbomite, nigerite, and taafeite minerals, European Journal of Mineralogy 14, 389-395</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Hogbömite-Zincohögbomite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.CB.20</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Oxide, Metal: Oxygen = 2: 3,3: 5, and similar, With medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Zincohogbomite-2N6S.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1952</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/hydroxylapatite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hydroxylapatite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/apatite"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | P | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">hexagonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">apatite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/hydroxylapatite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;OH</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Renamed</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Pentacalcium triphosphate hydroxyl</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1992</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1992:3"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1992.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(P&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;OH</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R050512 | R060180 | R100225 | R130713</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Hydroxylapatite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Hydroxylapatite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Named hydro-apatite: Damour A A (1856) Sur l'hydro-apatite, espèce minérale, Annales des Mines 10, 65-68 Renamed hydroxyapatite: Schaller W T (1912) Mineralogical notes, Series 2. Mineralogy of the French phosphorites, U.S. Geological Survey Bulletin 509, 89-100 Name changed from hydroxylapatite to apatite-(CaOH): Burke E A J (2008) Tidying up mineral names: an IMA-CNMNC scheme for suffixes, hyphens and diacritical marks, The Mineralogical Record 39, 131-135 Name changed from apatite-(CaOH) back to hydroxylapatite. In addition, apatite-CaOH)-M is renamed to hydroxylapatite-M and is defined as a monoclinic variant of hydroxylapatite and is not considered a distinct species: Pasero M, Kampf A R, Ferraris C, Pekov I V, Rakovan J R, White T J (2010) Nomenclature of the apatite supergroup minerals, European Journal of Mineralogy 22, 163-179</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Apatite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.BN.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions, without H2O, With only large cations, (OH, etc.):RO4 = 0.33:1</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Hydroxylapatite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
