    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Esperite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Esperite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Moore P B, Ribbe P H (1965) A study of “calcium-larsenite” renamed esperite, American Mineralogist 50, 1170-1178 Chemical formula revised from PbCa_3_Zn_4_(SiO_4_)_4_: Tait K T, Yang H, Downs R T, Li C, Pinch W W (2010) The crystal structure of esperite, with a revised chemical formula, PbCa_2_(ZnSiO_4_)_3_, isostructural with beryllonite, American Mineralogist 95, 699-705</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Beryllonite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.AB.15</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Nesosilicate without additional anions; cations in [4] and greater coordination</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Esperite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1964-027</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/moydite-y">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Moydite-(Y)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Y | B | O | H | C</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">orthorhombic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/moyditey.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">YB(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1985-025</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Yttrium boron tetrahydroxyl carbonate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2798</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2798:0"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2798.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">YB(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Moydite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Moydite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Grice J D, Van Velthuizen J, Dunn P J, Newbury D E, Etz E S, Nielsen C H (1986) Moydite (Y,REE)[B(OH)4](CO3), a new mineral species from the Evans-Lou Pegmatite, Quebec, The Canadian Mineralogist 24, 665-673 Hawthorne F C, Burke E A J, Ercit T S, Grew E S, Grice J D, Jambor J L, Puziewicz J, Roberts A C, Vanko D A (1988) New mineral names, American Mineralogist 73, 189-199 Name changed from moydite: Nickel E H, Mandarino J A (1987) Procedures involving the IMA Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names and guidelines on mineral nomenclature, American Mineralogist 72, 1031-1042</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>06.AC.45</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Monoborate, B(O,OH)4, without and with additional anions; 1(T), 1(T)+OH, etc</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Moydite-%28Y%29.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1985-025</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/ferrosaponite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ferrosaponite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Fe | Mg | Si | Al | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">smectite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;0.3&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;,Mg,Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Si,Al)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2002-028</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-29079</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:29079:7"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-29079.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;0.3&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;,Mg,Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Si,Al)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ferrosaponite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Ferrosaponite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Chukanov N V, Pekov I V, Zadov A E, Chukanova V N, Mökkel S (2003) Ferrosaponite Ca_0.3_(Fe^2+^,Mg,Fe^3+^)_3_·(Si,Al)_4_O_10_(OH)_2_·4H_2_O, the new trioctahedral smectite, Zapiski Vserossijskogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchestva 132(2), 68-74</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Smectite-vermiculite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.EC.45</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phyllosilicate with mica sheets, composed of tetrahedral and octahedral nets</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://webmineral.com/data/Ferrosaponite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>2002-028</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/cherepanovite">
