    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CaBe(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)(OH)</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Renamed</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Calcium beryllium phosphate hydroxyl</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1962</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1962:6"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1962.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CaBe(P&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)(OH)</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R050518 | R050520 | R060353 | R070451</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Hydroxylherderite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Hydroxylherderite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Originally named hydro-herderite: Penfield S L (1894) On the crystallization of herderite, The American Journal of Science 147, 329-339 Name changed to hydroxyl-herderite: Palache C, Berman H, Frondel C (1951) 41.5.4_2 Hydroxyl-herderite [CaBe(PO_4_)(OH,F)], in The System of Mineralogy, Volume II, Seventh Edition, John Wiley and Sons, Inc (New York) 820-822 Name changed from hydroxyl-herderite: Burke E A J (2008) Tidying up mineral names: an IMA-CNMNC scheme for suffixes, hyphens and diacritical marks, The Mineralogical Record 39, 131-135</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Gadolinite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.BA.10</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. with additional anions, without H2O, With small and medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Hydroxylherderite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1894</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
