    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Konishi H, Groy T L, Dodony I, Miyawaki R, Matsubara S, Buseck P R (2003) Crystal structure of protoanthophyllite: A new mineral from the Takese ultramafic complex, Japan, American Mineralogist 88, 1718-1723 Name changed from protoanthophyllite: Hawthorne F C, Oberti R, Harlow G E, Maresch W V, Martin R F, Schumacher J C, Welch M D (2012) Nomenclature of the amphibole supergroup. American Mineralogist 97, 2031-2048</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amphibole</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/stevensite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Stevensite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Na | Mg | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">smectite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/stevensite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca,Na)&lt;sub&gt;x&lt;/sub&gt;Mg&lt;sub&gt;3-y&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Questionable mineral species|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-3770</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:3770:5"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-3770.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca,Na)&lt;sub&gt;x&lt;/sub&gt;Mg&lt;sub&gt;3-y&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R070332</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Stevensite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Stevensite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">The mineral is described but not named: Leeds A R (1873) Contributions to mineralogy, American Journal of Science and Arts 6, 22-26 Name is published: Chester A H (1896) Stevensite, in A Dictionary of the Names of Minerals including their History and Etymology, John Wiley and Sons (New York) 257-257</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Clay</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.EC.45</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phyllosilicate with mica sheets, composed of tetrahedral and octahedral nets</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Stevensite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>0</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/plumbopharmacosiderite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Plumbopharmacosiderite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Pb | Fe | As | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">cubic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pb&lt;sub&gt;0.5&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(AsO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;·5H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2016-109</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pb&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;0.5&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(As&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;·5H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Plumbopharmacosiderite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Plumbopharmacosiderite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Vignola P, Rotiroti N, Hatert F, Dal Bo F, Gentile P, Albertini C, Merlini M, Risplendente A, Pavese A (2018) Plumbopharmacosiderite, Pb_0.5_Fe^3+^_4_(AsO_4_)_3_(OH)_4_·5H_2_O, a new mineral species from the Monte Faló Pb-Zn mine near the village of Coiromonte in the Armeno municipality, Novara Province, Italy. The Canadian Mineralogist 56, 143-150</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Pharmacosiderite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/franconite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Franconite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Nb | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">franconite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/franconite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaNb&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1981-006a</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Disodium tetraniobium undecaoxide nonahydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1595</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1595:6"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1595.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaNb&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R110185</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Franconite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Franconite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Jambor J L, Sabina A P, Roberts A C, Bonardi M, Ramik R A, Sturman B D (1984) Franconite, a new hydrated Na-Nb oxide mineral from Montreal Island, Quebec, The Canadian Mineralogist 22, 239-243 Chemical formula revised from Na_2_Nb_4_O_11_·9H_2_O: Haring M M M, McDonald A M (2014) Franconite, NaNb_2_O_5_(OH)·3H_2_O: structure determination and the role of H bonging, with comments on the crystal chemistry of franconite-related minerals. Mineralogical Magazine 78, 591-607</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.FM.15</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Hydroxide (without V or U), with H2O±(OH); unclassified</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Franconite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1981-006a</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/zigrasite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Zigrasite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Mg | Zr | P | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">MgZr(PO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2008-046</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Magnesium zirconium diphosphate tetrahydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-39007</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:39007:9"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-39007.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">MgZr&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;(P&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R120143</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Zigrasite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Zigrasite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Hawthorne F C, Ball N A, Nizamoff J W, Simmons W B (2009) Zigrasite, MgZr(PO_4_)_2_(H_2_O)_4_, a new phosphate mineral from the Dunton quarry, Newry, Oxford County, Maine, USA, Mineralogical Magazine 73, 415-420</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>08.CE.75</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Phosphate, etc. without additional anions, with H2O, With only medium-sized cations, RO4:H2O about 1:2.5</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>2008-046</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/lemmleinite-k">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lemmleinite-K</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | K | Ti | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">labuntsovite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;K&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;Ti&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(OH,O)&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;·8H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1997-003</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Renamed</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-7048</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:7048:1"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-7048.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;K&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(O,OH)&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;·8H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Lemmleinite-K</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Lemmleinite-K</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Khomyakov A P, Nechelyustov G N, Rastsvetaeva R K, Dorokhova G I (1999) Lemmleinite, NaK_2_(Ti,Nb)_2_Si_4_O_12_(O,OH)_2_·2H_2_O - a new mineral of the labuntsovite-nenadkevichite family, Zapiski Vserossijskogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchestva 128(5), 54-62 Name changed from lemmleinite to lemmleinite-K: Chukanov N V, Pekov I V, Khomyakov A P (2002) Recommended nomenclature for labuntsovite-group minerals, European Journal of Mineralogy 14, 165-173</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Labuntsovite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.CE.30d</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Cyclosilicate: [Si4O12]8- 4-membered single rings (vierer-Einfachringe), without insular complex anions</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Lemmleinite-K.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1997-003</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/minasgeraisite-y">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Minasgeraisite-(Y)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Be | Y | Si | O</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">gadolinite-datolite-gadolinite subgroup</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/minasgeraisitey.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CaBe&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Y&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1983-090</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2716</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2716:4"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2716.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">CaBe&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Y&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R120134</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Minasgeraisite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Minasgeraisite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Foord E E, Gaines R V, Crock J G, Simmons W B, Barbosa C P (1986) Minasgeraisite, a new member of the gadolinite group from Minas Gerais, Brazil, American Mineralogist 71, 603-607 Name changed from minasgeraisite: Nickel E H, Mandarino J A (1987) Procedures involving the IMA Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names and guidelines on mineral nomenclature, American Mineralogist 72, 1031-1042</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Gadolinite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.AJ.20</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Nesosilicate with BO3 triangles and/or B[4], Be[4] tetrahedra, cornersharing with SiO4</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Minasgeraisite-%28Y%29.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1983-090</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/novacekite-ii">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
