    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Renamed</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Al&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;20&lt;/sub&gt;·6H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R050091 | R050103</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Thomsonite-Ca</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Thomsonite-Ca</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Brooke H J (1820) On mesotype, needlestone, and thomsonite, Annals of Philosophy 16, 193-194 Name change from thomsonite, when thomsonite-Sr was discovered: Pekov I V, Lovskaya E V, Turchkova A G, Chukanov N V, Zadov A E, Rastsvetaeva R K, Kononkova N N (2001) Thomsonite-Sr (Sr, Ca)2Na[Al2Si5O20]·6–7H2O, a new zeolite mineral from Khibiny Massif (Kola Peninsula) and thomsonite-Ca—thomsonite-Sr an isomorphous series, Zapiski Vserossijskogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchestva 130, issue 4, 46-55</gsmin:statusnotes>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/barioperovskite">
