    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-58.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">K&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Ca[(U&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·5H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Agrinierite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Agrinierite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Cesbron F, Brown W L, Bariand P, Geffroy J (1972) Rameauite and agrinierite, two new hydrated complex uranyl oxides from Margnac, France, Mineralogical Magazine 38, 781-789 Chemical formula modified: Cahill C L, Burns P C (2000) The structure of agrinierite: a Sr-containing uranyl oxide hydrate mineral, American Mineralogist 85, 1294-1297</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Compreignacite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.GB.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Uranyl hydroxide, With additional cations (K, Ca, Ba, Pb, etc.); with mainly UO2(O,OH)5 pentagonal polyhedra</gsmin:strunzlabel>
