    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaCo&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;(S&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)(OH)&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;Cl·6H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Thérèsemagnanite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Theresemagnanite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Sarp H (1993) Guarinoite (ZnCoNi)_6_(SO_4_)(OH,Cl)_10_·5H_2_O et theresemagnanite (CoZnNi)_6_(SO_4_)(OH,Cl)_10_·8H_2_O, deux nouveaux minéraux de la mine de Cap Garonne, Var, France, Archives des Sciences, Genève 46, 37-44 Chemistry changed from Co_6_SO_4_(OH)_10_·8H_2_O: Hålenius U, Hatert F, Pasero M, Mills S J (2015) IMA Commission on New Minerals, Nomenclature and Classification (CNMNC) Newsletter 27. New minerals and nomenclature modifications approved in 2015. Mineralogical Magazine 79, 1223-1230</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Ktenasite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.DD.80</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sulfate, selenate, etc. with additional anions and H2O, With only medium-sized cations; sheets of edge-sharing octahedra</gsmin:strunzlabel>
