    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">BaCa&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)(V&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)(V&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;F</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Aradite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Aradite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Galuskin E V, Gfeller F, Galuskina I O, Pakhomova A, Armbruster T, Vapnik Y, Wlodyka R, Dzierzanowski P, Murashko M (2015) New minerals with a modular structure derived from hatrurite from the pyrometamorphic Hatrurim Complex. Part II. Zadovite, BaCa_6_[(SiO_4_)(PO_4_)](PO_4_)_2_F and aradite, BaCa_6_[(SiO_4_)(VO_4_)](VO_4_)_2_F, from paralavas of the Hatrurim Basin, Negev Desert, Israel. Mineralogical Magazine 79, 1073-1087</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Zadovite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/birchite">
