  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/lausenite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lausenite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Fe | S | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/lausenite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;·5H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Grandfathered|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: DiironIII trisulfate pentahydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2345</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2345:6"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2345.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(S&lt;sup&gt;6+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;·5H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Lausenite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Lausenite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Originally described with the name rogersite: Lausen C (1928) Hydrous sulphates formed under fumerolic conditions at the United Verde Mine, American Mineralogist 13, 203-229 Name changed to lausenite because rogersite was already in use: Butler G M (1928) Corrections to volume 13, American Mineralogist 13, 594-594 Chemical formula revised: Majzlan J, Botez C, Stephens P W (2005) The crystal structures of synthetic Fe&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(SO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O)&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt; and the type specimen of lausenite, American Mineralogist 90, 411-416</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>07.CB.70</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sulfate, selenate, etc. without additional anions, with H2O, With only medium-sized cations</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Lausenite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1928</gsmin:wikipediadate>
