  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Role">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Roles are played by a relata in a relation, e.g. a person plays the role of employee in an employs relation.  The relata playing the role is the RolePlayer and the other relata are RoleObjects. Because a role (Mary as employer, John as employee) is derived from a specific relation, e.g.  Mary employs John, it mutully depends on a specific reified relation instance (Relator - the employment of John by Mary). Roles carry qualities -  indeed, they are are a bundle of qualities.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Role  </rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Inherant"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n7bda25761fc44f8595ef751309700190b364"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n7bda25761fc44f8595ef751309700190b365"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n7bda25761fc44f8595ef751309700190b366"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:nodeID="n7bda25761fc44f8595ef751309700190b367"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="n7bda25761fc44f8595ef751309700190b368"/>
  </rdf:Description>
