    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Ce | Ti | P | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">orthorhombic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/laplanditece.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;CeTiPSi&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;·5H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1974-005</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2331</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2331:9"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2331.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Ce&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;P&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;·5H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Laplandite-(Ce)</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Laplandite-(Ce)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Eskova E M, Semenov E I, Khomyakov A P, Kazakova M E, Sidorenko O V (1974) Laplandite, a new mineral, Zapiski Vsesoyuznogo Mineralogicheskogo Obshchestva 103, 571-575 Name changed from laplandite: Nickel E H, Mandarino J A (1987) Procedures involving the IMA Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names and guidelines on mineral nomenclature, American Mineralogist 72, 1031-1042</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.DJ.10</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Inosilicate with 4-periodic double and triple chains</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Laplandite-%28Ce%29.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1974-005</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/rinkite-ce">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Rinkite-(Ce)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Ce | Na | Ti | Si | O | F</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;REE)Na(NaCa)Ti(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OF)F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Ce&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;)Na(NaCa)Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OF)F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R050229</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Rinkite-(Ce)</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Rinkite-(Ce)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Lorenzen J (1884) Untersuchung einiger mineralien aus Kangerdluarsuk in Grönland, Zeitschrift für Krystallographie und Mineralogie 9, 243-254 Rinkite is invalidated and assumed to be identical with mosandrite: Fleischer M (1958) New mineral names, American Mineralogist 43, 790-798 Revalidated as a mineral IMA2009-C: Bellezza M, Merlino S, Perchiazzi N (2009) Mosandrite: Structural and crystal-chemical relationships with rinkite, The Canadian Mineralogist 47, 897-908 Chemical formula revised: Cámara F, Sokolova E, Hawthorne F C (2011) From structure topology to chemical composition. XII. Titanium silicates: the crystal chemistry of rinkite, Na&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Ca&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;REETi(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;OF&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;, Mineralogical Magazine 75, 2755-2774 Name changed from rinkite: Sokolova E, Cámara F (2017) The seidozerite supergroup of TS-block minerals: nomenclature and classification, with change of the following names: rinkite to rinkite-(Ce), mosandrite to mosandrite-(Ce), hainite to hainite-(Y) and innelite-1T to innelite-1A. Mineralogical Magazine 81, 1457-1487</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Seidozerite-Rinkite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/haxonite">
