  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/rockobject/Fossil_Object">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">NOTE--this class is intended to represent individual fossil objects. If some kind of material fossils are granular constituents in a sedimentary rock, they should be represented using 'Biogenic_Granular_Material, with sub classes for different kinds of fossils, e.g. in crinoid grainstone, radiolarian chert, diatomite.</rdfs:comment>
