    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Thalénite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Thalenite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Benedicks C (1898) Thalénit, frän Österby i Dalarne, Geologiska Föreningens i Stockholm Förhandlingar 20, 308-312 Name changed from thalenite: Nickel E H, Mandarino J A (1987) Procedures involving the IMA Commission on New Minerals and Mineral Names and guidelines on mineral nomenclature, American Mineralogist 72, 1031-1042 Formula changed from Y_3_Si_3_O_10_(OH): Škoda R, Plášil J, Jonsson E, Copjaková R, Langhof J, Galiová M V (2015) Redefinition of thalénite-(Y) and discreditation of fluorthalénite-(Y): a re-investigation of type material from the Österby pegmatite, Dalarna, Sweden, and from additional localities. Mineralogical Magazine 79, 965-983</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.BJ.20</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sorosilicate with Si3O10, Si4O11, etc. anions; cations in octahedral [6] and greater coordination</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Thalenite-%28Y%29.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1898</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicunit/Geophysical_Unit">
