  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/timeMetBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source TimeRegion starts at the end of the target TimeRegion; there is no intervening time, and the boundary instants are distinct;  inverse of meets</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/timeDisjoint"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/timeYoungerThan"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/ischart/BaseCryogenianSP2016">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologiccontact/Stratigraphic_Point"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defined chronometrically; but will be replaced by GSSP. The new Cryogenian GSSP will be placed at a globally correlative level that lies stratigraphically beneath the first appearance of widespread glaciation and is assigned in the interim a ‘calibrated age’ of circa 720 Ma (Episodes Vol. 39, no. 1)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Stratotype Point Base of Cryogenian</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.18814/epiiugs/2016/v39i1/89231"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://stratigraphy.org/gssps/"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nc46de412defa4a2f8ad575fa1d491761b2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/hostedBy"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Rock_Body"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/hainite-y">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hainite-(Y)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Y | Na | Ti | Si | O | F</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">rosenbuschite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Y)Na(NaCa)Ti(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OF)F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Redefined|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">(Ca&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Y&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;)Na(NaCa)Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(OF)F&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R141183</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Hainite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Hainite-(Y)</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Blumrich J (1893) Die phonolithe des Friedländer Bezirkes in Nordböhmen, Tschermaks Mineralogische und Petrographische Mitteilungen 13, 465-495 Redefined: Johan Z, Cech F (1989) Nouvelles données sur la hainite, Na&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Ca&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;[(Ti,Zr,Mn,Fe,Nb,Ta)&lt;sub&gt;1.50&lt;/sub&gt;[box]&lt;sub&gt;0.50&lt;/sub&gt;(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;F&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; et ses relations cristallochimiques avec la götzenite, Na&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Ca&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Ti(Si&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;F&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;, Comptes Rendus de L’Académie des Sciences Paris 308, 1237-1242 Chemical formula redefined: Christiansen C C, Johnsen O, Makovicky E (2003) Crystal chemistry of the rosenbuschite group, The Canadian Mineralogist 41, 1203-1224 Chemical formula redefined again from Na(Na,Ca)_2_Ca_2_(Ca,Zr,Y)_2_Ti(Si_2_O_7_)_2_F_2_F_2_: Sokolova E (2006) From structure topology to chemical composition. I. Structural hierarchy and stereochemistry in titanium disilicate minerals. The Canadian Mineralogist 44, 1273-133 Name changed from hainite: Sokolova E, Cámara F (2017) The seidozerite supergroup of TS-block minerals: nomenclature and classification, with change of the following names: rinkite to rinkite-(Ce), mosandrite to mosandrite-(Ce), hainite to hainite-(Y) and innelite-1T to innelite-1A. Mineralogical Magazine 81, 1457-1487</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Seidozerite-Rinkite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/andyrobertsite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Andyrobertsite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>K | Cd | Cu | As | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
