  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/magnesio-hastingsite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Magnesio-hastingsite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Ca | Mg | Fe | Si | Al | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">amphibole-group 2 Ca</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;)(Si&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;)Si&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R040010 | R070145 | R070288</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Magnesio-hastingsite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Magnesio-hastingsite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Billings M (1928) The chemistry, optics, and genesis of the hastingsite group of amphiboles, American Mineralogist 13, 287-296 Redefined: Leake B E, Woolley A R, Arps C E S, Birch W D, Gilbert M C, Grice J D, Hawthorne F C, Kato A, Kisch H J, Krivovichev V G, Linthout K, Laird J, Mandarino J A, Maresch W V, Nickel E H, Rock N M S, Schumacher J C, Smith D C, Stephenson N C N, Ungaretti L, Whittaker E J W, Youzhi G (1997) Nomenclature of amphiboles: Report of the subcommittee on amphiboles of the International Mineralogical Association, commission on new minerals and mineral names, The Canadian Mineralogist 35, 219-246 Name changed from magnesiohastingsite: Hawthorne F C, Oberti R, Harlow G E, Maresch W V, Martin R F, Schumacher J C, Welch M D (2012) Nomenclature of the amphibole supergroup, American Mineralogist 97, 2031-2048</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amphibole</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/ernienickelite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ernienickelite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ni | Mn | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">hexagonal</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">chalcophanite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/ernienickelite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NiMn&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1993-002</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:iupacchemname xml:lang="en">IUPAC: Nickel trimanganeseVII heptaoxide trihydrate</gsmin:iupacchemname>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1402</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1402:7"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1402.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ni&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;Mn&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;·3H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ernienickelite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Ernienickelite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Grice J D, Gartrell B, Gault R A, Van Velthuizen J (1994) Ernienickelite, NiMn_3_O_7_·3H_2_O, a new mineral species from the Siberia Complex, Western Australia: comments on the crystallography of the chalcophanite group, The Canadian Mineralogist 32, 333-337</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.FL.20</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Hydroxide (without V or U), Hydroxides with H2O±(OH); sheets of edge-sharing octahedra</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Ernienickelite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1993-002</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/bubnovaite">
