  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/tremolite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tremolite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Mg | Fe | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">amphibole-group 2 Ca</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/tremolite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;Ca&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;5.0-4.5&lt;/sub&gt;Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;0.0-0.5&lt;/sub&gt;)Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Redefined</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-4011</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:4011:8"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-4011.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&lt;span style="border: 1px solid #333; font-size:7px;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;Ca&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mg&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Si&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R040045 | R040109 | R050167 | R050173 | R050210 | R050498 | R060311 | R061087 | R070422 | R150094</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Tremolite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Tremolite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Mineral is mentioned by its name, but not described: Höpfner J G A (1789) Ueber die Klassifikation der Fossilien in einem Schreiben des Herausgebers an Herrn Dr. Karsten in Halle, Magazin für die Naturkunde Helvetiens 4, 255-332 Named by E Pini, as described, for instance, in: Delamétherie J C (1792) Observations et mémoires sur la physique, sur l’histoire naturelle, et sur les arts et métiers. Discours préliminaire, Observations sur la Physique, sur l’Histoire Naturelle et sur les Arts 40, 2-40 Redefined: Leake B E, Woolley A R, Arps C E S, Birch W D, Gilbert M C, Grice J D, Hawthorne F C, Kato A, Kisch H J, Krivovichev V G, Linthout K, Laird J, Mandarino J A, Maresch W V, Nickel E H, Rock N M S, Schumacher J C, Smith D C, Stephenson N C N, Ungaretti L, Whittaker E J W, Youzhi G (1997) Nomenclature of amphiboles: Report of the subcommittee on amphiboles of the International Mineralogical Association, commission on new minerals and mineral names, The Canadian Mineralogist 35, 219-246</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amphibole</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.DE.10</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Inosilicate with 2-periodic double chains, Si4O11; Clinoamphiboles</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Tremolite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1789</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
