  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/rockobject/Crust">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A planet's crust, e.g. the Earth's crust. Is a rock object as it is constituted only by solid geologic material. Surprisingly, is a stratigraphic unit, because dependent spatially and temporally on the upper mantle rock object. This means it cannot be moved (e.g. to another planet) and retain identity, and it must always be younger and over the upper mantle.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Crust</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Geologic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
