    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologictime/Age"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Generic_Geologic_Time_Unit"/>
    <gsoc:timeStarts rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologictime/BasePhanerozoic"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fortunian is the earliest of the five Siberian Early Cambrian ages, and also the most recently recognized. The stage and its equivalents were only added to the Cambrian in 1992. http://palaeos.com/paleozoic/cambrian/fortunian.html</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Interval for grouping all specific instances of the Fortunian Age</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The name 'Fortunian Stage' is proposed as the lowest stage of the Cambrian and the lower part of the proposed Terreneuvian Series. The base of the Fortunian Stage corresponds to the defined GSSP for the base of the Cambrian (FAD of Trichophycus pedum and base of the T. pedum Zone [ichnofossils] in the Fortune Head section, Burin Peninsula, Newfoundland, Canada). Its top will be defined by the base of the overlying stage, which is presently undefined. Prepared by E. Landing for ISCS, January 2007; http://www.palaeontology.geo.uu.se/ISCS/ISCS_Terreneuvian_Fortunian_2007.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fortunian Age</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/zincrosasite">
