  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/nyboite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nybøite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Mg | Al | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">amphibole-group 4 Na</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/nyboite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaNa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)(Si&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;Al)O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Redefined|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-2944</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:2944:1"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-2944.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">NaNa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(Mg&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;)(Si&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;Al)O&lt;sub&gt;22&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Nybøite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Nyboite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Ungaretti L, Smith D C, Rossi G (1981) Crystal-chemistry by X-ray structure refinement and electron microprobe analysis of a series of sodic-calcic to alkali-amphiboles from the Nybö eclogite pod, Norway, Bulletin de Minéralogie 104, 400-412 Fleischer M, Chao G Y, Mandarino J A (1982) New mineral names, American Mineralogist 67, 854-860 Redefined: Leake B E, Woolley A R, Arps C E S, Birch W D, Gilbert M C, Grice J D, Hawthorne F C, Kato A, Kisch H J, Krivovichev V G, Linthout K, Laird J, Mandarino J A, Maresch W V, Nickel E H, Rock N M S, Schumacher J C, Smith D C, Stephenson N C N, Ungaretti L, Whittaker E J W, Youzhi G (1997) Nomenclature of amphiboles: Report of the subcommittee on amphiboles of the International Mineralogical Association, commission on new minerals and mineral names, The Canadian Mineralogist 35, 219-246</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Amphibole</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.DE.25</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Inosilicate with 2-periodic double chains, Si4O11; Clinoamphiboles</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Nyboite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1981</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/djerfisherite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Djerfisherite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>K | Fe | Cu | Ni | S | Cl</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">cubic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:fleischersgroup xml:lang="en">djerfisherite</gsmin:fleischersgroup>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/djerfisherite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">K&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe,Cu,Ni)&lt;sub&gt;25&lt;/sub&gt;S&lt;sub&gt;26&lt;/sub&gt;Cl</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA1965-028</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-1299</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:1299:3"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-1299.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">K&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;(Fe,Cu,Ni)&lt;sub&gt;25&lt;/sub&gt;S&lt;sub&gt;26&lt;/sub&gt;Cl</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R070390</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Djerfisherite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Djerfisherite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Fuchs L H (1966) Djerfisherite, alkali copper-iron sulfide: A new mineral from enstatite chondrites, Science 153, 166-167 Chemical formula revised from K&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(Na.Cu)(Fe,Ni)&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;S&lt;sub&gt;14&lt;/sub&gt;: Dmitrieva M T, Ilyukhin V V (1976) Crystal structure of jerfisherite, Soviet Physics - Doklady 20, 469-470 Chemical formula revised again: Henderson C M B, Kogarko L N, Plant D A (1999) Extreme closed system fractionation of volatile-rich, ultrabasic peralkaline melt inclusions and the occurrence of djerfisherite in the Kugda alkaline complex, Siberia, Mineralogical Magazine 63, 433-438</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Djerfisherite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>02.FC.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Other sulfide with Cl, Br, I (halide-sulfides)</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Djerfisherite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1965-028</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/jankovicite">
