    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Mertieite-II</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Mertieite-II</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Originally named mertierite: Desborough G A, Finney J J, Leonard B F (1973) Mertieite, a new palladium mineral from Goodnews Bay, Alaska, American Mineralogist 58, 1-10 Redefined and renamed: Cabri L J, Laflamme J H G, Stewart J M, Rowland J F, Chen T T (1975) New data on some palladium arsenides and antimonides, The Canadian Mineralogist 13, 321-335 Chemical formula revised from Pd_8_(Sb,As)_3_: Karimova O V, Zolotarev A A, Evstigneeva T L, Johanson B S (2018) Mertieite-II, Pd_8_Sb_2.5_As_0.5_, crystal-structure refinement and formula revision. Mineralogical Magazine 82, S247-S257</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Stillwaterite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>02.AC.15b</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sulfide or sulfosalt alloy of metalloids with PGE</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Mertieite-II.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1973</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
