  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Plasma">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">a gas of ions, atoms or molecules which have one or more orbital electrons stripped (or, rarely, an extra electron attached), and free electrons.  Whether a given degree of ionization suffices to call the substance "plasma" depends on a specific phenomenon being considered. In other words, plasma is a matter which cannot be correctly described without the presence of charged particles taken into account. (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasma_(physics))</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Plasma</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Fluid"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="ndb26e920196f4af8bbd263b193e6f242b1079">
