    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Pb&lt;sub&gt;47&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;24&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;13&lt;/sub&gt;Cl&lt;sub&gt;25&lt;/sub&gt;(BO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Mereheadite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Mereheadite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Welch M D, Criddle A J, Symes R F (1998) Mereheadite, Pb_2_O(OH)Cl: a new litharge-related oxychloride from Merehead Quarry, Cranmore, Somerset, Mineralogical Magazine 62, 387-393 Chemical formula revised: Krivovichev S V, Turner R, Rumsey M, Sidra O I, Kirk C A (2009) The crystal structure and chemistry of mereheadite, Mineralogical Magazine 73, 103-117</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>03.DC.45</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Double-, Oxy- or Hydroxy-  halide with Pb (As,Sb,Bi), without Cu</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Mereheadite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1996-045</gsmin:wikipediadate>
