    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Bindi L, Biagioni C, Martini B, Salvetti A, Fontana G D, Taronna M, Ciriotti M E (2016) Tavagnascoite, Bi_4_O_4_(SO_4_)(OH)_2_, a new oxyhydroxy bismuth sulfate related to klebelsbergite. Mineralogical Magazine 80, 647-657</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Klebelsbergite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/cebollite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cebollite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Al | Si | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/cebollite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Questionable mineral species|Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-924</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:924:7"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-924.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;Al&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(SiO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Cebollite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Cebollite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Larsen E S, Schaller W T (1914) Cebollite, a new mineral, Journal of the Washington Academy of Sciences 4, 480-482</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Melilite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>09.BB.10</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Sorosilicate: Si2O7 groups, without non-tetrahedral anions; cations in tetrahedral [4] and greater coordination</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Cebollite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>0</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/chinchorroite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chinchorroite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Na | Mg | As | O | H</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">triclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mg&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(As&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(AsO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O)&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imanumber xml:lang="en">IMA2017-106</gsmin:imanumber>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved|Pending publication</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Na&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mg&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(As&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(As&lt;sup&gt;5+&lt;/sup&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;OH)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O)&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Chinchorroite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Chinchorroite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Kampf, A.R., Nash, B.P., Dini, M. and Molina Donoso, A.A. (2018) Chinchorroite, IMA 2017-106. CNMNC Newsletter No. 42, April 2018, page 448; Mineralogical Magazine, 82, 445–451</gsmin:statusnotes>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/brannerite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Brannerite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>U | Ti | O</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic, amorphous</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/brannerite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">UTi&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-754</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:754:0"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-754.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">U&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;Ti&lt;sup&gt;4+&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffids>R060613 | R080091</gsmin:rruffids>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Brannerite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Brannerite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Hess F L, Wells R C (1920) Brannerite, a new uranium mineral, Journal of the Franklin Institute 189, 225-237</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:structuralgroup xml:lang="en">Brannerite</gsmin:structuralgroup>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>04.DH.05</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Oxide, Metal: Oxygen = 1:2 and similar, With large (+- medium-sized) cations; sheets of edge-sharing octahedra</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Brannerite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1920</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Unit_Of_Measure_Value"/>
    <skos:altLabel>M</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>m</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The metric and SI base unit of distance.  The 17th General Conference on Weights and Measures in 1983 defined the meter as that distance that makes the speed of light in a vacuum equal to exactly 299 792 458 meters per second. The speed of light in a vacuum, \(c\), is one of the fundamental constants of nature. The meter is equal to approximately 1.093 613 3 yards, 3.280 840 feet, or 39.370 079 inches.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en-us">Meter</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Metre</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicsetting/Marine_Carbonate_Platform_Setting">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dct:source xml:lang="en">CGI Event Environment vocabulary</dct:source>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A shallow submerged plateau separated from continental landmasses, on which high biological carbonate production rates produce enough sediment to maintain the platform surface near sea level. Grades into atoll as area becomes smaller and ringing coral reefs become more prominent part of the setting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">marine carbonate platform setting</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicsetting/Marine_Setting"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb91377c629b1476ba973ba249cd56575b56"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicfoliation/discrete_disjunct_spaced_cleavage">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Disjunct spaced cleavage defined by discrete cleavage surfaces, typically in low-grade clastic rocks. Syn. Fracture cleavage.</rdfs:comment>
    <dct:source xml:lang="en">Neuendorf et al. 2005, Borradaile et al. 1982.</dct:source>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">discrete disjunct spaced cleavage</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geologicfoliation/spaced_cleavage"/>
  </rdf:Description>
