  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/mineral/carboborite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Carboborite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/geology/Mineral_Material"/>
    <gsmin:chemistryelements>Ca | Mg | B | O | H | C</gsmin:chemistryelements>
    <gsmin:crystalsystem xml:lang="en">monoclinic</gsmin:crystalsystem>
    <gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>http://www.handbookofmineralogy.com/pdfs/carboborite.pdf</gsmin:handbookofmineralogyurl>
    <gsmin:imachemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mg[B(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:imachemistry>
    <gsmin:imastatus xml:lang="en">Approved</gsmin:imastatus>
    <gsmin:mindatid>min-891</gsmin:mindatid>
    <gsmin:mindaturi rdf:resource="https://www.mindat.org/1:1:891:0"/>
    <gsmin:mindaturl>http://www.mindat.org/min-891.html</gsmin:mindaturl>
    <gsmin:rruffchemistry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Ca&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;Mg[B(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O</gsmin:rruffchemistry>
    <gsmin:rruffnamehtml rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">Carboborite</gsmin:rruffnamehtml>
    <gsmin:rruffnameplain xml:lang="en">Carboborite</gsmin:rruffnameplain>
    <gsmin:statusnotes xml:lang="en">Hsieh H T, Chien T C, Liu L P (1964) The new mineral carboborite, MgCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)(B&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;)·10H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O, Scientia Sinica 13, 813-821 Chemical formula revised from MgCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;(CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;)(B&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;)·10H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O to MgCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;[CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;[B(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O: Ma Z, Shi N, Shen J, Peng Z (1981) The refinement of the crystal structure of carboborite MgCa&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;[CO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;[B(OH)&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;]&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;·4H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;O, Bulletin de Minéralogie 104, 578-581</gsmin:statusnotes>
    <gsmin:strunzcodeV10>06.AC.50</gsmin:strunzcodeV10>
    <gsmin:strunzlabel xml:lang="en">Monoborate, B(O,OH)4, without and with additional anions; 1(T), 1(T)+OH, etc</gsmin:strunzlabel>
    <gsmin:webmineralurl>http://www.webmineral.com/data/Carboborite.shtml</gsmin:webmineralurl>
    <gsmin:wikipediadate>1964</gsmin:wikipediadate>
  </rdf:Description>
