  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/granularmaterial/Single_Crystal_Particle_Material">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Typical grain constituent in a phaneritic igneous or metamorphic rock, visible to naked eye or with hand lense. Particle are individual mineral grains that have crystallized from melt or through metamorphic processes.  In deformed rocks, these my have some subgrain structure but at the scale of description are considered individual particles in a granular material constituent of a rock.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">mono-mineralic crystal particle </rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/granularmaterial/Crystallized_Particle_Material"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n1fd689c41a864089b476a4d481ba57bdb90">
